SD=~/.claude/skills/rework-mr/scripts; cd {SRC}/agent-skills-demo
python3 $SD/threads.py propose t1 --iid 3 --says needs --why 'Miriam asks to rename the comments factory `queryKeys` to `commentKeys`, matching `discussionKeys`. The export is used in `getComments.ts`, `createComment.ts` and `deleteComment.ts` plus its own definition, so the rename is mechanical. **Recommendation:** do the rename.' --outcome fix --plan 'Rename `queryKeys` to `commentKeys` in `query-keys.ts` and its three call sites.' --change - <<'CHANGE_EOF'
@@ src/features/comments/api/query-keys.ts:1-4
export const commentKeys = {
  all: ['comments'] as const,
  list: (discussionId: string) => [...commentKeys.all, discussionId] as const,
};
CHANGE_EOF
python3 $SD/threads.py quote t1 --focus --iid 3

SD=~/.claude/skills/rework-mr/scripts; cd {SRC}/agent-skills-demo
python3 $SD/threads.py propose t2 --iid 3 --says needs --why 'Miriam is right: `discussionKeys.detail` returns `['\''discussion'\'', id]`, which shares no prefix with `discussionKeys.all` (`['\''discussions'\'']`), so `refetchQueries` on `all` in `updateDiscussion.ts:62` skips the detail query. Her option 1 is cheap here: every use of the detail key goes through `discussionKeys.detail` (`getDiscussion.ts`, `updateDiscussion.ts`), so changing the factory touches no other call site. Exact-key `setQueryData` on `all` in create/delete is unaffected; their invalidation of `all` now also covers details, which is the intent. Option 2 would keep the footgun in the factory. **Recommendation:** option 1, make `detail` extend `all`.' --outcome fix --answer-now --plan 'Change `discussionKeys.detail` to `[...discussionKeys.all, discussionId]`, so refetching `all` includes the detail query, and answer Miriam that option 1 needs no other call-site changes.' --change - <<'CHANGE_EOF'
@@ src/features/discussions/api/query-keys.ts:1-4
export const discussionKeys = {
  all: ['discussions'] as const,
  detail: (discussionId: string) => [...discussionKeys.all, discussionId] as const,
};
CHANGE_EOF
python3 $SD/threads.py quote t2 --focus --iid 3
